{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["Divination in their hand — they were bringing types of divination to Balaam lest he say, 'I have no instruments of divination in my hand.' As it is written: ״he stood with his divination arrows, he consulted the terafim, he examined the liver\" — [referring to] 'בימינו היה הקסם' — it was in his right hand."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The quotation 'בימינו היה הקסם' appears to be drawn from the subsequent verse (Numbers 22:7 continued or a paraphrase); its placement and attribution within the comment are somewhat ambiguous, so I have translated it as an interjected gloss. The scriptural quotation without address follows Rashbam's usual practice of citing without reference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:45.315535687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}